.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ngx-auth-add 1  "ngx-auth-add " 
.SH NAME
ngx\-auth\-add \- Add a user, or change their password (asked twice, or read from stdin with \-\-password\-stdin)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBngx\-auth\-add\fR [\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISITE\fR> <\fIUSER\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add a user, or change their password (asked twice, or read from stdin with \-\-password\-stdin)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR
Read the password from the first line of stdin
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISITE\fR>
Site ID or domain
.TP
<\fIUSER\fR>

.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  sudo ngx auth add 4 alice
  echo "$PASS" | sudo ngx auth add 4 ci \-\-password\-stdin
